WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.280
Grogu, or as he's affectionately known,&nbsp;
"Baby Yoda," has been through a lot even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.720
though he's only fifty years old. The&nbsp;
former Padawan and now surrogate son to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:15.000
everyone's favorite Mandalorian has had quite&nbsp;
the adventures across the galaxy far far away.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:20.400
The entire "Star Wars" universe takes place&nbsp;
in a galaxy far, far away, so it has its own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.780
way of measuring history. Since it's one of the&nbsp;
most important events in the galaxy's history,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:31.380
"Star Wars" uses BBY (Before the Battle of Yavin)&nbsp;
and ABY (After the Battle of Yavin) to mark time.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:35.400
The Battle of Yavin takes place in&nbsp;
"Star Wars Episode IV – A New Hope."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.240
It's when Luke Skywalker joins a group&nbsp;
of courageous Rebel Alliance fighters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:43.440
to attack the Death Star. While this is a&nbsp;
smaller battle by "Star Wars" standards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:48.480
it holds significant weight — Luke blasts the&nbsp;
planet-destroying would-be omega weapon into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.740
space dust, and the loss of the Death Star&nbsp;
stands as a major setback for the Empire.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:58.320
"The Mandalorian" begins in 9 ABY. That's&nbsp;
25 years before "The Force Awakens" and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:02.640
five years after the events of "Return of the&nbsp;
Jedi." Now that the Empire has been defeated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:08.100
the Rebel Alliance is trying to rebuild the galaxy&nbsp;
peacefully. Meanwhile, the Mandalorians are still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:12.480
spread out and without a home. Din Djarin is&nbsp;
saved by a group of religious Mandalorians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:17.460
who train him in their ways as a bounty hunter.&nbsp;
However, his entire life changes when he accepts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:22.380
a mission to collect a mysterious package for the&nbsp;
now-fallen members of the Empire. He discovers the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:27.420
package is baby Grogu and decides to save him&nbsp;
rather than let the Empire experiment on him.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:35.040
Grogu was likely born in the same year as Anakin&nbsp;
Skywalker, 41 BBY, making him 50 years old by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:39.780
time "The Mandalorian" begins. This tracks, as&nbsp;
Din is initially told that he must retrieve a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:44.820
50-year-old asset and deliver him to his client.&nbsp;
However, when he finds Grogu, he sees that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:49.680
looks and acts like a baby. There's a reason&nbsp;
for this — Grogu is the same species as Yoda.

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:52.860
In the show, Mando is told that&nbsp;
this species ages differently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:56.340
and could live for centuries. But&nbsp;
that's about all we know about them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:00.660
"Star Wars" creator George Lucas admitted&nbsp;
to MovieFone that when he created Yoda,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:05.160
the Jedi Master was designed to fill the void&nbsp;
left by Obi-Wan Kenobi's death in "A New Hope."

00:02:05.499 --> 00:02:07.059
"I'm looking for a Jedi Master."

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:13.380
"Oh, a Jedi Master. Yoda. You seek Yoda."

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.660
Lucas knew that he needed someone to train Luke,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:20.100
so he made Yoda without much thought to&nbsp;
any background for his species. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:23.760
he quite liked how the ambiguity&nbsp;
gives Yoda an aura of mystery.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:27.600
In keeping that mystery alive, "The&nbsp;
Mandalorian" showrunners Dave Filoni&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:32.520
and Jon Favreau decided to honor Lucas'&nbsp;
original idea of Yoda's past being a mystery.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:37.980
Season 2 of "The Mandalorian" gives audiences&nbsp;
more information regarding Grogu's enigmatic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:41.280
past. As it's established that&nbsp;
he's 50 years old and a Jedi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:45.960
it stands to reason that Grogu would be around&nbsp;
during the Clone Wars as a Padawan. Luckily,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:48.840
the show does not disappoint&nbsp;
when detailing Grogu's timeline.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:54.840
Grogu shares with Ahsoka Tano that he was raised&nbsp;
in the Jedi Temple on Coruscant, and in 19 BBY,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.840 --> 00:03:01.020
he witnessed and survived Order 66. Ahsoka deduces&nbsp;
that someone protected him and took him out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:05.760
the Temple, but everything after that is murky&nbsp;
as Grogu has seemingly blocked those memories.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:10.680
Order 66 is a dark moment in "Star Wars"&nbsp;
history. It's when the Empire enacts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:14.520
inhibitor chips that have been installed&nbsp;
in every clone trooper's brain. They were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:17.460
put in the clones to prevent them from&nbsp;
being too aggressive given that their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:22.620
genetic source material came from Jango Fett.&nbsp;
However, the Empire uses the chips to dictate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:27.060
the clones' behavior patterns, and in the&nbsp;
words of clone trooper Fives, the chips are,

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:34.858
"Built into our genetic code to make us do&nbsp;
whatever someone wants…. Even kill the Jedi."

00:03:34.858 --> 00:03:40.000
Across various "Star Wars" properties, audiences&nbsp;
have witnessed the brutality of Order 66,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:44.880
from "Revenge of the Sith," "The Clone Wars,"&nbsp;
and even in video games like "Star Wars Jedi:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:50.563
Fallen Order." And we can add "The Mandalorian"&nbsp;
to that list, as poor Grogu saw it all go down.

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:54.259
With the Empire hunting down the&nbsp;
remaining Jedi after Order 66,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.259 --> 00:03:58.920
Grogu has an excellent reason to keep his head&nbsp;
down during those years. Perhaps as a result,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:03.000
not much is known about his time before&nbsp;
meeting Mando. One thing is clear, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:07.020
once the rebels take down the Empire, the&nbsp;
remainder of the evil government begins&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:11.040
looking for Grogu so they can experiment&nbsp;
with his midi-chlorians. At some point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:15.900
they successfully capture him before he's taken&nbsp;
by Nikto mercenaries. This is when the Imperials&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:21.000
commission Mando to retrieve Grogu and return him&nbsp;
to their scientists for further testing. Luckily,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:25.080
Djarin chooses to save Grogu instead, and&nbsp;
the two have been on the run ever since.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:30.540
How the Nikto mercenaries manage to capture Grogu&nbsp;
from the Imperials is unclear, but once word&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:35.100
spreads that they have him, it becomes an all-out&nbsp;
battle for Mando to safely retrieve the Child.

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:39.540
However, there is an internet theory out there&nbsp;
that suggests the Nikto mercenaries are actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:44.220
the good guys. After all, they rescue Grogu&nbsp;
from the Imperials and fight to protect him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:48.600
against the bounty hunters looking to collect.&nbsp;
Perhaps the mercenaries could be prisoners or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:52.440
former slaves of the Empire laying down&nbsp;
their lives to protect an innocent child&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:56.670
from being delivered the same fate they&nbsp;
experienced at the hands of the Imperials.

00:04:56.670 --> 00:05:01.560
Season 2 of "The Mandalorian" really ties together&nbsp;
the "Star Wars" universe. Not only does it pull&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:05.880
on events from the films, but it also brings in&nbsp;
characters from "The Clone Wars" with live-action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:10.860
actors. In Episode 3, "The Heiress," Mando&nbsp;
meets Bo-Katan Kryze from "The Clone Wars."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:16.140
She teaches Mando more about Mandalorian culture&nbsp;
and eventually shares her knowledge of the Jedi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:20.580
as she fought with them once upon a time. She&nbsp;
points him in the direction of Ahsoka Tano,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:23.400
which results in her long&nbsp;
overdue live-action debut.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:28.440
Once Mando brings Grogu to Ahsoka, she ultimately&nbsp;
decides not to train the little one to become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:33.960
a Jedi. Shocked, Mando questions why, as his&nbsp;
entire goal at this point is reuniting Grogu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:38.580
with his people, the Jedi. She tells him that&nbsp;
Grogu has grown too attached to Mando and that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:43.980
a Jedi with a strong attachment is dangerous. She&nbsp;
saw firsthand how Anakin's unhealthy relationship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:49.560
and attachment to Padmé brings about his downfall,&nbsp;
and she vows not to let Grogu down that road.

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:54.360
Interestingly, Ahsoka sees this attachment&nbsp;
in Grogu immediately, as she knows that his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:58.740
destiny is not to become a Jedi. However, it&nbsp;
takes Luke time to come to this realization,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:02.520
as he takes Grogu to train him at&nbsp;
the end of Season 2. Ultimately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:06.900
Luke discovers that Grogu's heart isn't&nbsp;
in it, and lets him decide which path he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:11.481
wants to follow: training to be a Jedi&nbsp;
or to be with his father, Din Djarin.

00:06:11.481 --> 00:06:16.440
Once Ahsoka refuses to train Grogu, she leaves&nbsp;
Mando with some hope, telling him to take the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:20.700
Child to meditate at the seeing stone on the&nbsp;
planet Tython. She shares that the stone has a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:25.140
strong connection to the Force and that Grogu can&nbsp;
use it to reach out to any other Jedi close by.

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:29.400
Mando and Grogu travel to Tython where&nbsp;
he's ambushed by Imperials looking to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:33.660
capture Grogu. Luckily, Mando manages&nbsp;
to partner with Boba Fett and fellow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:37.680
bounty hunter Fennec Shand to fight&nbsp;
against the soldiers. Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:43.204
Grogu is successfully captured, resulting in Mando&nbsp;
planning a daring rescue of his little friend.

00:06:43.204 --> 00:06:48.334
"Soon. He will be back with me."

00:06:48.781 --> 00:06:54.078
"He means more to me than you will ever know."

00:06:54.078 --> 00:06:57.240
And while the two are eventually&nbsp;
reunited, the team is trapped by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.240 --> 00:07:01.740
Moff Gideon's Dark Troopers. Luckily, Grogu&nbsp;
managed to connect with a Jedi after all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:06.120
as Luke comes to rescue the team. He tells&nbsp;
Grogu that he will take him away to train,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:09.780
which results in an emotional&nbsp;
farewell between Grogu and Mando.

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:14.820
As Mando is part of an extremely religious sect&nbsp;
of Mandalorians, he isn't supposed to remove his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:19.020
helmet in the presence of others. However,&nbsp;
he chooses to remove it so that he can look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:23.940
Grogu in the eye to say goodbye. This act of love&nbsp;
between pseudo-father and son holds significant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:28.500
weight for Mando, as once his helmet has been&nbsp;
removed, his role as a Mandalorian within his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:34.378
sect is now void. However, he doesn't care. In&nbsp;
this case, a proper goodbye is more important.

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:38.220
Once Grogu makes his decision to leave&nbsp;
Luke and his Jedi training behind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:42.840
he is reunited with Mando. Together, the two&nbsp;
form their own little clan. At this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:45.660
it looks like Mando is gearing&nbsp;
up to restore the Mandalorians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:49.818
and get them back to their home world of&nbsp;
Mandalore in "The Mandalorian" Season 3.

00:07:49.818 --> 00:07:54.078
"My people are scattered,&nbsp;
like stars in the galaxy."

00:07:54.078 --> 00:07:58.260
Both Mando and Grogu make conscious decisions&nbsp;
to pick each other over everything else,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.260 --> 00:08:01.860
regardless of the ramifications.&nbsp;
They see each other as family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:06.240
which gives "The Mandalorian" a thematic link&nbsp;
to the broader "Star Wars" universe. Right from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:09.780
the beginning, the bonds of family,&nbsp;
especially father-son relationships,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:14.220
are one of the franchise's most prominent&nbsp;
themes. As far as the films go, the broken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:18.720
connections of the Skywalker family unit are&nbsp;
the primary force pushing the story forward.

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:23.160
"The Mandalorian" is telling a new tale about&nbsp;
the bonds of a father-son relationship between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:28.320
Mando and Grogu. Much like Luke is willing to&nbsp;
sacrifice himself for his father in "Return of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:33.420
Jedi," Grogu and Mando are willing to sacrifice&nbsp;
everything they know for each other. Grogu takes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:38.997
a pass on becoming a Jedi, and Mando removes his&nbsp;
helmet and forfeits his position as a Mandalorian.

00:08:38.997 --> 00:08:42.900
Season 2 of "The Mandalorian" ends with&nbsp;
the triumphant return of Luke Skywalker.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.900 --> 00:08:47.940
And while a much older version of Luke appears&nbsp;
in 2015's "The Force Awakens" and its sequels,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:52.020
seeing Luke during his prime in the days&nbsp;
following the events of "Return of the Jedi"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:57.060
was a treat for some fans. However, at the time,&nbsp;
it was pretty disappointing how Luke didn't meet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.060 --> 00:09:01.740
Ahsoka. She was Anakin's apprentice, and likely&nbsp;
never knew that he turned back to the light&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:06.000
side right before he met his end. Luckily,&nbsp;
"The Book of Boba Fett" fixes all of this.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:10.800
Just when everyone is settling into Boba Fett's&nbsp;
series on the sandy hills of Tatooine, Mando&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:15.540
arrives to tie up loose ends in preparation for&nbsp;
his next season. For audiences, a Mando-centric&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:19.980
episode in the middle of Boba Fett's show felt&nbsp;
a little unusual, but who are we to argue?

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:23.880
That being said, audiences finally got&nbsp;
to watch a conversation between Luke and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:27.960
Ahsoka where she reminisces on how much&nbsp;
he reminds her of his father, to which he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:32.040
responds with a knowing look. She offers him&nbsp;
words of wisdom as Luke wonders what he should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:36.780
do next. She cautions Luke about the strong&nbsp;
bond between Grogu and Mando before leaving,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:41.601
as fans are left to wonder if the two will ever&nbsp;
share the screen again in her upcoming series.

00:09:41.601 --> 00:09:46.380
As "The Mandalorian" continues, we predict more&nbsp;
of Grogu's story will be uncovered. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:51.720
one thing will likely stay the same: the mystery&nbsp;
surrounding his species. As mentioned previously,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:56.880
Grogu is a member of the same species as Jedi&nbsp;
Master Yoda. Yoda is an incredibly powerful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.880 --> 00:10:02.100
extremely wise Jedi in "Star Wars" lore.&nbsp;
However, most people don't realize that aside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:06.000
from Yoda and Grogu, there's another member&nbsp;
of their species featured in the timeline.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:10.800
Initially shown in "The Phantom Menace," Yaddle&nbsp;
is a Jedi council member and is present during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:15.240
the evaluation of a young Anakin Skywalker.&nbsp;
However, by "Attack of the Clones," she has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.240 --> 00:10:20.160
disappeared. Luckily, Yaddle's disappearance is&nbsp;
expanded upon in "Star Wars: Tales of the Jedi."

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:25.140
In the Disney+ series, she steps down from her&nbsp;
position on the Jedi High Council following&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:30.600
the events of the Battle of Naboo in the year 32&nbsp;
BBY. After learning that Count Dooku won't attend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:35.940
the funeral of his old Padawan Qui-Gon Jinn she&nbsp;
grows suspicious of his actions. Yaddle follows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:39.900
Dooku and learns that he's turned to the dark&nbsp;
side of the Force. When she confronts him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:44.400
she offers Dooku compassion, which makes&nbsp;
it all the sadder when Dooku kills her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:50.400
thus solidifying his place next to his Master,&nbsp;
Darth Sidious, also known as…Emperor Palpatine.

